<title>USA: United Industrial Corp Q3 net falls.</title>
<headline>United Industrial Corp Q3 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter Ended	     Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>			    September 30,	  September 30,</p>
<p>			1996	  1995	   1996	   1995</p>
<p>Net Sales  $54,159,000 $53,568,000 $163,925,000 $163,090,000</p>
<p>Income before income</p>
<p>  taxes	   220,000     991,000    4,912,000    5,145,000</p>
<p> Income taxes    57,000     568,000    1,860,000    2,258,000</p>
<p> Net income     163,000     423,000    3,052,000    2,887,000</p>
<p>Net earnings per share</p>
<p>			  .01	   .04	    .25	    .24</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>outstanding</p>
<p>		 12,212,000  12,221,000   12,198,000   12,204,000</p>
<p>NOTES: 1996 figures include a charge of $2.2 million for an agreement in principle reached with certain officials of the U.S. Navy to resolve a dispute over the SH-60 program to upgrade helicopter training simulators. Net income in Q3 1996, excluding the charge reached $1514,000, or $0.12 cents per share.</p>
<p>	 -- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
